# Tests excluded from the CI xfstests runs (.github/workflows/xfstests.yml
# and .github/workflows/xfstests-uml.yml).
#
# One test per line, in xfstests -E format (e.g. "generic/003").
#
# A test goes in here only with a comment saying why, and the why must be a
# understood reason -- a server-side capability the loopback export does not
# have, a test that is meaningless against NFS, a genuine bug with a link to
# where it is tracked. "It was red" is not a reason; an unexplained failure
# should stay red until someone explains it.

# generic/258 and generic/634: explicit timestamps lost under an NFSv4.2
# timestamp delegation. Kernel bug, client and knfsd together.
#
# Seen with delegations on, on v7.2.6 and master under UML and on the
# runner's 6.17 kernel. Passes with delegations off on every kernel, and
# with delegations on on v6.18.52 (v6.12.57 was reported passing too).
#
# When the open of a file is granted a write delegation with delegated
# timestamps (OPEN_DELEGATE_WRITE_ATTRS_DELEG), nfs_setattr()
# (fs/nfs/inode.c) keeps a utimensat() by the owner on the client and sends
# no SETATTR. The times reach the server only at DELEGRETURN, as
# TIME_DELEG_ACCESS/TIME_DELEG_MODIFY. knfsd's nfsd4_vet_deleg_time()
# (fs/nfsd/nfs4state.c) ignores a delegated time earlier than the file's
# time at grant and clamps one in the future to the current time. A written
# file with no accepted time is then stamped to now by
# nfsd4_finalize_deleg_timestamps().
#
# Traced with scripts/00-run-xfstests-in-uml.sh TRACE_EVENTS: the file's
# OPEN gets nfsd_deleg_write, no client SETATTR follows the touch, and at
# unmount nfsd_vfs_setattr applies ia_valid=DELEG with no time bits
# (dropped) or with ATIME_SET|MTIME_SET (clamped). The tests only fail
# after earlier tests in -g quick have run; alone, the file gets no write
# delegation and a plain SETATTR carries the times.
#
# generic/258 sets a 1960 atime/mtime: dropped as earlier than grant.
# generic/634 sets 1901 and year 0 (dropped) and 2038..year 2147483647
# (clamped to now).
#
# Fix: "[PATCH v3 0/3] fs/nfsd: accept a backdated timestamp from a
# delegation holder" (Jeff Layton, 2026-09-04),
# https://ratatoskr.run/linux-fsdevel/2026/09/17514664/t
# It makes knfsd accept a backdated delegated time, which covers
# generic/258 and 634's two past dates. Per the series, "nfsd still clamps a
# future time", so generic/634's future dates are not covered by it and 634
# is expected to keep failing with delegations on.
generic/258
generic/634

# generic/444: NFSv3 with POSIX ACLs drops setgid on a new subdirectory of a
# setgid directory with a default ACL, when the creator is not in its group.
# The client sends MKDIR, then a separate SETACL as that user, and the
# server's posix_acl_update_mode() clears S_ISGID for a non-member. Local
# filesystems apply the inherited ACL during mkdir and keep the bit, which
# is what the test expects. An NFSv3 protocol limitation: MKDIR cannot carry
# an ACL, so the server cannot tell this SETACL belongs to the create.
# Reproduced by hand on master with vers=3.
generic/444
